- op: discuss  # 2012
  at: '2026-08-21T17:13:38Z'  # 2012
  by: agent  # 2012
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2012
  clock: 3  # 2012
  nonce: '2012'  # 2012
  message: "SATISFIED with behavioral evidence re-run on the MERGED tree at dev be48477b74 (PR #462), not on the feature branch.\n\nLIVE REPRO, merged tree, openzeddelin-contracts:\n  solidity dispatches_to = 877   (was 0)\n  solidity kinds: method=3051, function=5\n  call_site nodes = 1250         (regression check, see below)\n\nThe statement asked that a Solidity contract function participate in type-hierarchy dispatch as a Java or Ruby method does. It now does: 877 edges where there were none, with the 5 remaining kind=function symbols being file-scope free functions, which are correctly NOT members.\n\nINDEPENDENT EVIDENCE: test_interface_dispatch_parity's solidity cell was a STRICT xfail naming this cause. It XPASSed and is retired. That gate has now given up two cells this cycle -- ruby to INV-nosoz, solidity to this item -- and neither retirement was authored by the same work that filed the cell.\n\nTHE FIX IS CONTAINMENT, NOT A RENAME. A function with an enclosing contract/interface/library is a method; a file-scope free function (Solidity 0.7+) stays a function. constructor, modifier and event keep their own kinds. A discriminating control test pins the file-scope case as still producing no dispatch, so an unconditional rename could not pass as this fix.\n\nA REGRESSION I INTRODUCED AND THEN REPAIRED, recorded because the failure mode is reusable. The first cut fixed the four kind==function literals inside solidity.py and passed every test, including five edge-survival controls written to catch exactly a missed reader. The corpus then showed calls down 6,689 (-43%) and 1,249 nodes gone: a FIFTH and SIXTH copy in hypergumbo_core.linkers.solidity_abi, in ANOTHER PACKAGE, filtering on (function, constructor). It silently stopped minting ABI call-site nodes -- the JS-to-Solidity boundary -- with nothing raised; a count simply dropped. Both packages now read one SOLIDITY_CALLABLE_DECLARATION_KINDS in core, pinned from the producer side by a test in the producer's own package. The call_site count of 1250 above is the standing check that the repair held.\n\nRATCHET: the G1 runtime_coherence gate correctly breached, because (method/solidity -> method/solidity) began carrying dispatches_to alongside overrides. That partition became visible BECAUSE the fix worked -- before, it carried only overrides and so was never an offender. Allow-listed as legitimate (overrides runs child->parent, dispatches_to parent->child: opposite directions over one endpoint shape), following the WI-duguk rust-trait precedent. The baseline was NOT raised; it stays 1.\n\nIDENTITY, DISCLOSED NOT HIDDEN: kind is a slot in both Symbol.id and the typed stable_id, so contract-member ids CHANGE. Treated as a producer correction rather than a scheme change -- the formula is untouched and the input is now correct -- and recorded in CHANGELOG as a regenerate-do-not-diff caveat. If a future ruling wants a scheme version on this, the change is small and the boundary is a single commit.\n\nNOT CLAIMED: I did not measure whether the 877 new dispatch edges improve any downstream view (slice seeds, ranking centrality, dead-code). They are structurally correct edges that did not exist; their consumer-level value is unmeasured."  # 2012
